    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Issues Found and Fixed\n\n### 1. **governance.test.js** - Missing named exports\n**Problem**: The test expected to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from the governance module, but it was only available in the default export.\n\n**Fix**: Added named exports in `/packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js` for:\n- `APPROVAL_STATUSES`\n- `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`\n- `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`\n- `RISK_LEVELS`\n\nThese are now available as both named and default exports, maintaining backwards compatibility.\n\n### 2. **eval/index.test.js** - Toxicity metric signature mismatch\n**Problem**: The `runEvaluations` function calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`, but `toxicityMetric` has the signature `(outputs, bannedTerms)`. When references were passed as the second argument, they were treated as banned terms, causing both outputs to be incorrectly flagged as toxic (score 0 instead of 1).\n\n**Fix**: Wrapped `toxicityMetric` in `DEFAULT_METRICS` with an arrow function that only passes outputs, not references:\n```javascript\nexport const DEFAULT_METRICS = [\n  exactMatchMetric,\n  (outputs, references) => toxicityMetric(outputs),  // wrapper to only pass outputs\n  lengthVarianceMetric\n];\n```\n\nThis maintains backwards compatibility\u2014direct calls to `toxicityMetric` still work with the original signature.\n\n**Test Results**: \u2705 All 28 tests passing across 8 test files.",
